    "result_text": "Tests are green. I agreed with all three findings and restructured accordingly:\n\n1. **`countInCity` moved to the right unit** \u2014 the per-city count loop now lives on the `OwnerCity` helper (`OwnerCity.countInCity(city, ownerRepository)`), next to the normalization it depends on. Both `CheckCityCapacity` and `FlagCityCapacityWarning` now depend on the helper rather than on each other, keeping the step classes as pure single-`service` units. Removed the now-unused `Owner` import from `CheckCityCapacity`.\n\n2. **`WARNING_THRESHOLD` relocated** \u2014 it now sits on `FlagCityCapacityWarning` (the warning's own concern), referencing `CheckCityCapacity.CAPACITY` for the shared upper bound. `CAPACITY` stays on `CheckCityCapacity` where the hard check reads it.\n\n3. **Stale javadoc fixed** \u2014 `OwnerCity`'s class comment no longer claims a single consumer; it now names both the capacity check and the capacity warning, reached through `countInCity`.\n\nAcceptance behaviour is unchanged (same counting semantics, same `[40, 49]` warning window, same hard rejection at 50), and the suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
